  "Date": "2026-09-21T11:21:56Z",
  "Message": "fix(auth): a trusted origin's foreign Bearer is the client's login, not a bad key\n\nWith trustLoopback/trustTailnet enabled, a client that sent its OWN\nupstream credential as `Authorization: Bearer` — Claude Code in OAuth mode\n(claude.ai token), Codex (ChatGPT token) — was refused 401 \"Invalid proxy\nAPI key\", although the origin needs no key at all; the 401 then made the\nclient drop its login. From a trusted origin an unrecognised Bearer now\nreads as \"no key\". An explicit x-api-key keeps failing loudly (a rotated\nkey must be noticed), untrusted origins are unchanged, the Bearer grants\nno management access, and both credential headers are still stripped\nbefore anything goes upstream.\n\nTests cover both fixes, including raw WebSocket handshakes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "c8f76a184c76d8691f0aba230e14d7f441e5e85b:test/auth-gate-websocket.test.js:generic-api-key:89"
 },
